>>And is it correct that the gender of Dirk, Lucrezia, Izchak and the
>>tool-shopkeepers are fixed, but all others may have random gender? 
> 
> For some values of "random". If the first pass (level ID plus a
> start-time-dependent number between -4 and +12, plus 18 if that's
> negative) is within the range of shopkeepers, then the gender will be
> determined according to whether that's odd or even; in other words,
> Kabalebo will always be male, Wonotobo will always be female. If it
> falls through to the second pass which chooses one from
> all-except-the-last-choice randomly, then the gender is _still_
> determined by the first pass's parity; likewise the third pass. In
> these cases, non-usual gender assignments can occur.

So on low levels the gender will always be deterministic.

Number of shopkeeper-names
--------------------------
shkliquors 	: 30
shkbooks	: 26
shkarmors	: 30
shkwands	: 31
shkrings	: 32
shkfoods	: 32
shkweapons	: 32
shktools	: 31 + OS-specific-number
shkgeneral	: 30	

So on a lucky day the start-time-dependent number is big enough
so that deep in the dungeon:

   (levelId + start_time_number > (num shk-names for the shop-type)

for non-tool shops.

(For tool-shops I'm not so sure if that's the case for all platforms.
But, because tool-shopkeepers always have fixed gender, it doesn't
matter anyway.)

